30,2,,status,Mio,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
31,2,,status,Toshio,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
32,2,,status,Jonathan,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
33,2,,status,Takumi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
34,2,,status,Kenji,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Mio,,"Most of our costs are fixed—hall hire and insurance. Plus, many people struggle to pay the full amount upfront.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,It's worse than we thought. Turnout dropped after the summer door charges. People stopped feeling like the evenings belonged to them.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Takumi,,"Exactly! A tiny group does all the work and attends everything, while others barely show up but pay the same. It's unfair.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"Chasing small payments is a nightmare. The treasurer spent six hours a month on it. Also, named grades caused friction in the past.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Kenji,,Newcomers are scared of the big upfront cost. Many taster guests won't join because they can't commit to a whole year.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Mio,,"If we have high fixed costs, we can't just charge per event, or we'll go broke if turnout is low.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Takumi, I understand the unfairness, but if we charge per event, we create a psychological barrier that keeps people away.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Takumi,,But why should the regulars subsidize people who never come? We need a system that reflects actual usage.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Takumi, any system with frequent small payments will kill the next treasurer. We need something streamlined.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"And we can't have ""grades"" or ""levels."" It creates a hierarchy that makes the club feel less inclusive.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Mio,,"We need a balance. We need the money guaranteed, but we can't ignore that some people need payment plans.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"If we make it a ""pay-as-you-go"" system, the regulars will feel the cost every single time they walk through the door.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Takumi,,"Then maybe a tiered system? High usage for those who come every week, and a low fee for the occasional visitors.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Takumi, the records show that named grades caused social friction. People in the lower tier stopped volunteering.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Kenji,,I agree with Toshio. Let's not label people. But we have to find a way to let people join mid-year easily.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Mio,,"So we have a conflict: fixed costs vs. accessibility, and fairness vs. administrative ease.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,The most important thing is that members feel welcome to attend without calculating the cost in their heads.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Takumi,,"I still think the current ""everyone pays the same"" is a recipe for resentment among the core members.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Toshio,,"Whatever we choose, it must not involve the treasurer spending their entire month chasing pennies.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Kenji,,Let's look at the options and see which one hurts the fewest people.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,,status,Mio,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
56,3,,status,Toshio,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
