59,3,,status,Kenji,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
60,3,1,talk,Mio,,"Option A is the safest for the budget, but Kenji's data shows it scares off newcomers and those with tight budgets.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,Option C is the worst for attendance. We already saw turnout drop when we tried door charges this summer.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Takumi,,Option B solves the fairness issue. People pay for the level of access they actually use.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Toshio,,"Option B is a nightmare to manage and, as I found, creates social divisions. Option A is the only one that saves the treasurer.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"Option C is the most welcoming for newcomers, but I worry it makes the club feel like a business.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Mio,,"@Toshio, if we go with A, can we allow monthly installments? The bank statements show people really need that.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"I strongly oppose C. We need to remove the ""weighing up"" process before every meeting.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Takumi,,"If we don't go with B, how do we address the fact that nine people do all the work?","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Toshio,,By keeping the administration simple so the volunteers aren't burdened with bookkeeping. I vote for A.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Kenji,,I can't support A if it keeps new people out. But B feels too rigid. Maybe C is the only way?,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Mio,,"C is too risky for our fixed costs. If we have a quiet month, we can't pay the insurance. I'm leaning toward A.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,"I agree with Mio. A flat fee, perhaps with a payment plan, ensures the club survives and members just show up.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Takumi,,"I still feel B is the only fair way, but if it causes ""friction"" as Toshio says, maybe it's not worth it.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Toshio,,"It isn't. The social cost of tiers is too high, and the admin cost of activity-based charging is impossible.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Kenji,,"If we go with A, we must promise to be flexible with how people pay. Otherwise, it's too exclusive.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Mio,,I'll support A if we agree to be flexible with installments. It's the only way to guarantee our fixed costs.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,I vote for A. It protects the atmosphere of the club.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Takumi,,"I'll concede to A, provided we find another way to thank the regulars who do the work.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Toshio,,A is the only logical choice for the treasurer's sanity.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Kenji,,"I'll go with A too, as long as we make the payment plans official for the newcomers.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
